# Line endings, decided here rather than by whoever cloned the repo.
#
# Git's default on Windows is `core.autocrlf=true`, which rewrites every text
# file to CRLF on checkout. That is invisible until something reads a file as
# *text it searches*, and this repo does that a lot: the desktop crates assert
# on their own source and on the bundled UI through `include_str!`, and a needle
# containing `\n` matches nothing in a file whose lines end `\r\n`.
#
# It cost three pushes to find, because the failures only appear on the Windows
# job and only for needles where the newline is in the middle -- `find("\nfn ")`
# still matches inside `"\r\nfn "`, so most of them survived and two did not.
# The tests normalise on their way in as well; this is the half that means they
# never see CRLF to begin with.
#
# `eol=lf` rather than `text=auto`: auto only normalises what git guesses is
# text, and the guess is per-file.
*.rs        text eol=lf
*.toml      text eol=lf
*.lock      text eol=lf
*.html      text eol=lf
*.css       text eol=lf
*.js        text eol=lf
*.mjs       text eol=lf
*.ts        text eol=lf
*.tsx       text eol=lf
*.json      text eol=lf
*.py        text eol=lf
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
*.md        text eol=lf
*.swift     text eol=lf
Makefile    text eol=lf

# Windows' own script hosts are the exception. `cmd.exe` is genuinely fussy
# about line endings in batch files, and there is no reason to make PowerShell
# differ from every other file a Windows developer opens.
*.bat       text eol=crlf
*.cmd       text eol=crlf

# Binary, so git never tries to translate anything inside them.
*.png       binary
*.icns      binary
*.ico       binary
*.woff2     binary
*.zip       binary
*.dmg       binary

# Committed build output. Both are copies of the esbuild bundle, kept in the
# tree so a browser can load the SDK without a build step, and held byte-exact
# by a `git diff --exit-code` in ci.yml. Marking them generated keeps them out
# of diffs and language stats, and out of what GitHub's analyses report on --
# a finding in a file you are not allowed to edit is noise by construction.
lemma-typescript/public/lemma-client.js linguist-generated=true
lemma-typescript/public/lemma-ui.js     linguist-generated=true
